{"base_rate":0.20767195767195767,"brier":0.1342165343915344,"bss":0.1843137585997895,"bss_hi":0.2808893604748968,"bss_lo":0.07066456019306512,"chart":{"base":[331.3,67.6],"fp":[235.2,227.5],"lead":"62,221 272,185.1 482,140 692,69.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.18 — higher than 26% of cities","fp":"low end +3pp, high end +32pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.4 °C — better than 19% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 3%; promised 79% → rained 56%"},"rel":"67.3,454.5 198.4,297.2 558.2,223.2"},"country":"US","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09130952380952377,"ess":473.0537562889719,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Dallas</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Dallas rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (95%), believe about\n<b>53%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 756 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nDALLAS 2.7 WNW, 3.6 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.18, ranked 157 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(110&ndash;178) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>364</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>88</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'><b>26%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'><b>53%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>62%</td><td class='num'><b>60%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>95%</td><td class='num'><b>53%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Dallas</b> <span class=\"muted\">United States</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.18</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>110&ndash;178\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>756 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Dallas &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Dallas\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.48626373626374,380.0 71.19454545454545,353.04545454545456 103.46831168831169,306.3636363636364 167.1181081081081,229.51351351351352 278.9971428571429,117.27272727272725 395.417894736842,22.78947368421052 395.417894736842,51.52631578947364 278.9971428571429,193.02727272727273 167.1181081081081,308.2162162162162 103.46831168831169,363.09090909090907 71.19454545454545,382.0 58.48626373626374,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"306.4074074074074\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"306.4074074074074\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.48626373626374,377.0 71.19454545454545,353.04545454545456 103.46831168831169,287.4545454545455 167.1181081081081,190.1621621621622 278.9971428571429,164.54545454545456 395.417894736842,190.42105263157896\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 1% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 364 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.48626373626374\" cy=\"377.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 8% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 88 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"71.19454545454545\" cy=\"353.04545454545456\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 13%&amp;#10;It rained 26% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"103.46831168831169\" cy=\"287.4545454545455\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 31%&amp;#10;It rained 53% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"167.1181081081081\" cy=\"190.1621621621622\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 62%&amp;#10;It rained 60% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"278.9971428571429\" cy=\"164.54545454545456\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 95%&amp;#10;It rained 53% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"395.417894736842\" cy=\"190.42105263157896\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(21%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Dallas the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.32) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.00).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>18%</td><td class='num'>-0.003</td><td class='num'>11.0%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.145</td><td class='num'>14.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'>0.184</td><td class='num'>1.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'>0.319</td><td class='num'>1.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":32.78306,"lon":-96.80667,"n":756,"n_cities":213,"name":"Dallas","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0013736263736263737,"n":364,"obs":0.013736263736263736,"sig":true},{"hi":0.07,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.03727272727272727,"n":88,"obs":0.07954545454545454